<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Pátzcuaro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patzcuaro">Pátzcuaro</a> is a highland lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michoacan">Michoacán</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, at about 2,000 metres above sea level. Its basin was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire">Purépecha</a> state, with the capitals Pátzcuaro, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ihuatzio">Ihuatzio</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tzintzuntzan">Tzintzuntzan</a> on its shores, and its island of Janitzio is famous for Day of the Dead celebrations. The lake has shrunk and suffered pollution in recent decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-patzcuaro.jpg" alt="Lake Pátzcuaro" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Gengiskanhg assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PatzcuaroLakeIslands_fromTheTopOfJanitzioIsland_PatzcuaroLake_MichoacanMexico.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
